# Strapi Content Model Migration Discipline

- Treat Strapi content-type schema changes as contract changes, not internal refactors.
- Before changing a field name/type/requiredness, identify all frontend/API consumers and migration impact.
- Prefer additive changes first (add new field, backfill, then deprecate old field) over destructive renames.
- Avoid changing `singularName`, `pluralName`, and endpoint identity unless explicitly approved (breaks route contracts).
- Keep `internal-docs/API_ENDPOINT_DESIGN.md` aligned with any model or query-contract changes.
- Regenerate and verify Strapi generated types after schema updates.
- For enum changes, ensure frontend constants and filters are updated in the same change.
- For content migrations, define rollback strategy and verify existing content still renders safely.
